// semantic_key.dl -- the pinned Souffle 2.5 stateful functor ABI for building
// semantic keys inside a generated program.
//
// A witness names its result and input by semantic key, so a key built by
// Souffle and a key built by the C++ canonicalizer must be the same bytes.
// These functors are the only sanctioned way to produce key material: each
// one emits exactly one type-tagged, length-prefixed field via
// SemanticKeyCodec. Only the resulting encoded fields may then be joined with
// `cat`, after a header. Concatenating raw cells -- with or without a
// separator -- is forbidden, because a cell could then move a field boundary.
//
// Each functor is pure and reentrant. The C++ side exports these exact
// C-linkage names with signature
//
//   souffle::RamDomain name(souffle::SymbolTable*, souffle::RecordTable*, ...)
//
// The implementation and the mandatory generated-program comparison land with
// the production Souffle executor in M8R.4; this file pins the contract the
// bundles below are written against.
//
// This ABI is six functors. The M8R plan originally specified three (symbol,
// number, unsigned) and was amended to match after review.
//
// The codec distinguishes five domains, so the Datalog side needs a primitive
// per tag or it cannot produce byte-identical keys. Collapsing stable ids into
// the symbol functor would let a symbol cell reading "memref:sha256:x" produce
// the same key as an id cell with that text; collapsing enum ordinals into the
// number functor would erase the difference between an epistemic state and a
// plain integer. The header is separate so the relation name and arity cannot
// be confused with a leading data field.

.functor veritas_key_header_v1(relation:symbol, arity:unsigned):symbol stateful
.functor veritas_key_id_v1(value:symbol):symbol stateful
.functor veritas_key_field_symbol_v1(value:symbol):symbol stateful
.functor veritas_key_field_number_v1(value:number):symbol stateful
.functor veritas_key_field_unsigned_v1(value:unsigned):symbol stateful
.functor veritas_key_field_enum_v1(value:number):symbol stateful

// Every bundle emits the same witness relation. It is relation-independent by
// construction: the canonicalizer validates and selects proofs without knowing
// what any particular result means.
.decl Witness(result_key:symbol, rule_id:symbol, input_key:symbol,
              input_ordinal:unsigned)
.output Witness(IO=csv, filename="Witness.csv")
